\newlabel{fig:shap_dep_dist_road}{{23a}{93}{SHAP dependence plot for \texttt {dist\_road} (distance to the nearest road). Road distance is the highest-ranked South America RF feature by mean absolute SHAP value. Its mean SHAP contribution is $-0.018$ and 19.6\% of sampled observations are positive, indicating that the road-accessibility axis more often enters as a suppressing term in the sampled risk distribution. Colour indicates the SHAP value of a secondary interacting feature.\relax }{figure.caption.91}{}}
